WEBVTT

00:02:56.496 --> 00:03:00.413
Or the cohort group could’ve been composed
of people who shop at health food stores

00:03:00.454 --> 00:03:03.871
and have different diets
or better access to healthcare.

00:03:04.163 --> 00:03:07.913
These factors that can affect results,
in addition to the factor being studied,

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:10.079
are known as “confounding variables”.

00:03:10.121 --> 00:03:13.038
These two major pitfalls,
combined with more general dangers,

00:03:13.079 --> 00:03:16.496
such as conflicts of interest 
or selective use of data,

00:03:16.538 --> 00:03:20.329
can make the findings of any particular 
epidemiological study suspect,

00:03:20.371 --> 00:03:22.454
and a good study must go out of its way

00:03:22.496 --> 00:03:26.204
to prove that its authors have taken steps
to eliminate these types of errors.

00:03:26.371 --> 00:03:29.954
But even when this has been done,
the very nature of epidemiological studies

00:03:29.996 --> 00:03:32.496
which examine differences
between preexisting groups